+      "text": "# Reuse solutions before rebuilding them\n\nRequested on 4 October 2026. Add this as a discovery step within the shared building protocol: before implementing a common feature, search the catalogue of solved problems and reusable components, read the matched component's instructions, and reuse or deliberately adapt it. It supplements the build process; it is not a new mandatory hold on every command.\n\n## First entries\n\n1. Live conversational voice: GPT Live (`gpt-live-1`), using Columbo's existing native transport and local service as the starting point. Extract a component only after checking the current voice repair. Provide one independent consuming example to prove it is usable outside Columbo.\n2. Live transcription: catalogue the actual implementations and their limits. Distinguish realtime input text, archived recording transcription, partial/final text, corrections and saved provenance. No provider or reusable module is selected yet.\n3. Chat interfaces: inventory existing interfaces, session/message models, streaming and reconnect behaviour, and ownership/licence constraints before choosing one to reuse. No general drop-in chat UI is verified yet.\n\n## What each entry should contain\n\n- Job phrases and boundaries: what it solves, when to use it and nearby jobs it does not solve.\n- Maintained code location, version, owner, supported platforms and dependencies; distinguish existing app code from an extracted package.\n- A minimal working example, configuration, permissions and failure/recovery behaviour; no embedded secrets or surprise microphone activation.\n- Evidence: unit/integration tests, an independent consuming app, known limitations and the date/platform of real device checks.\n- Links to the relevant build-stage instructions, with adoption notes and regression cases so later fixes improve future builds.\n\n## Live voice extraction plan\n\nSeparate the audio connection and events from the application controller. Define inputs (provider/session configuration, voice, consent and application callbacks) and outputs (transcript fragments, connection state, audio/reply status and errors). Preserve correct cancellation, opening/resume behaviour, bounded context updates and idempotent delegated replies.\n\nStart with the native iOS/WebRTC and Python-service stack that exists in Columbo. Do not call it a web, macOS or arbitrary coding-session integration until each host has its own example and tests. A direct voice connection to a Codex/Claude session needs a verified host adapter and result ownership; a phone interview waiter is not a general live-session bridge.\n\nAcceptance: a minimal second consumer can install the module and complete start, turn-taking, interruption, mute, long reply, disconnect/reconnect, resume and end without importing Columbo's interview state. Test physical audio separately, preserve the current app and recovered answers, run independent Astra/Fable reviews and Understudy, and document remaining limits. The work is queued; this document is not evidence that extraction is finished.\n\n## Routing and catalogue work\n\nColumbo question delivery and live voice integration are separate published capabilities, with job-led routes, since r000006. A provider-specific voice regression test must not be converted into Syrinx narration. Both-client benchmarks retain positive narration cases and nearby live-conversation/test cases. Build guidance now includes this discovery step; the standalone component remains queued.\n"
